WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.868
-Our next guest
has his stand-up special

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.734
"Practicing?" available
now on YouTube.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:09.200
Please welcome the very funny
Jesus Trejo!

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:16.868
♪♪

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:19.467
-Thank you. Thank you.
Please have a seat.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:23.734
Have a seat, you guys.
Thank you so much.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:27.067
I tipped my Uber driver 50 bucks
cash. Yeah.

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.400
You don't do something like that
and not tell anyone, so...

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.400
So I'll tell you guys.
I tipped him 50 bucks

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.234
because I wanted him to pretend
we were a family

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.300
when he dropped me off
at the airport.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.534
He was good, man.
He got out. We hugged.

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.434
He stood there and waved
at me aggressively.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:45.501
And as I'm walking away, I'm
pretending to be embarrassed.

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:48.834
I'm like, "Alright, man, chill."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.534
Ten minutes later,
he sends me a text.

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:51.801
"Are you at the gate yet?"

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.033
I mean, this transaction's over,
bro.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:59.200
I'm excited.
I'm back in the gym.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.100
I started going back.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.300
I made the mistake of asking
for a personal trainer.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.000
Don't do that.
The buffest guy came out.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.300
He goes, "It's 150."
I'm like, "Stop right there.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.567
I don't care if it's a day,
month or year.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:15.000
Not interested."
They need a cheaper option.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.234
Like, give me a chubby
personal trainer.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:22.200
Someone who I can build
with together.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.734
How much is it?
Accountability, bro.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:24.767
Let's do this.

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:30.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:33.167
What does a personal trainer do?
Count?

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:34.767
You're there bench-pressing.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.467
"One!"
That's what I said, man.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.000
My biggest pet peeve
is when they spot

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.367
you using their index finger.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.133
I hate that. They're like,
"There you go, there you go.

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.434
All you, all you.
There you go, there."

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:49.367
Then why are you here?
I paid for the whole hand.

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:50.367
Use the whole hand.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.067
I feel like if you have
a chubby personal trainer,

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.200
any question they ask you,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.467
you can answer by
asking it right back.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:01:59.534
"Are you going to be
here tomorrow?"

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:02.133
Bro, are you going to
be here tomorrow?

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.300
"Are you eating what
you're supposed to?"

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.200
Bro, are you eating
what you're supposed to?

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.968
Yeah, there's a guy
that goes to my gym

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.968
and he shadow boxes,
like for hours.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.567
He goes there.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.601
I want to go up to him like,
"Bro,

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.234
you have that machine at home."

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:19.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:21.868
"Go home.
Take the push-up guy with you."

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:23.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.300
Thank you.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:32.100
I feel like you have to be super
optimistic to be a shadow boxer.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.501
Have you ever seen
a shadow boxer lose?

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:39.501
They always win.
Like, if I did it, I would lose.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:42.133
Ooh, ooh, ooh.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:44.334
"Are you okay?"
Man, you should have seen
my shadow, bro.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:45.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.934
It's a big shadow, man.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.367
I've never been --

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.400
I've never been
to an escape room,

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.834
but I feel like
I would suck at them.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.501
It took me 35 years to move out
of my parents' apartment.

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:00.667
So what am I going
to do with one hour?

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:02.868
That's stressful.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:05.067
There's a lot that goes
into escaping a room.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:08.467
Finances,
your mother's blessing.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:09.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:12.701
I was going to go to one,
and I went to the website first

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:15.334
and the website said,
"If you can't figure it out,

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:17.701
don't worry,
we let you right out."

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.734
I'm like, that's B.S.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:23.734
If I pay $30 and I don't
solve it, leave me here.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:26.200
Bring the next group in.
Come on, have a seat, you guys.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.968
They'll walk in.
"Do you work here?"

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.434
No. I couldn't solve the puzzle.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:31.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.501
Thank you.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:36.200
"I couldn't solve the puzzle.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.133
Yeah. I haven't been
to work in a week.

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.234
Can you help me?"

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:43.501
The concept of escape rooms
to me is very funny.

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:45.767
Like, your life
is that good that you have

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:49.100
extra time and money
for more problems?

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.534
It's like, I'm going to turn my
apartment into an escape room.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.767
It's like I got to figure out
how to get dad health insurance.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.334
Time starts now. Go for it.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:04:01.834
[ Laughter and applause ]
Thank you, thank you.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.300
Oh, man, you guys are the best.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.467
[ Applause continues ]

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.701
I just got a jury summons.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.000
Yeah, they're sending
them out right now.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.734
So when you go home,
don't check your mailbox.

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.834
Yeah, I just got a jury
summons in the mail.

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:16.267
And you know
what's interesting?

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:21.300
That the jury summons landed
on the same day I have court.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.467
So we'll see.

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.834
Fingers crossed I get to be
a juror on my case.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:29.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:31.567
I'll be there for sure. Like,
"Your Honor, I know that guy.

00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:33.667
He's a good guy, that guy.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:36.367
He wouldn't even fight
his own shadow."

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:38.067
My name's Jesus Trejo.
That's my time.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:39.367
Thank you guys so much.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.434
-Thank you, buddy.

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:48.000
Jesus Trejo!

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.601
"Practicing?" is available
now on YouTube.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:51.968
We'll be right back, everybody.

